# Sort keys: builder A builds the true transform prefix.
name: sortkeys-builder-a-hook
kind: module
module: 39
region: code
address: 0x0307d87e
gate: build refuses unless the stock bytes at the target equal `expect`;
  the finished image must also pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale: Replaces the 0x30-byte inline fold loop of key builder A
  (function 0x0307d80a) with mov r0, r5 / bl cave_pfx /
  b.w 0x0307d8ae (the stock loop exit), NOP-padded. r5 is the
  record pointer at this site. Stock's loop uppercased ASCII
  a-z only, over exactly the first 4 characters: no accent
  fold, no leading-'The ' handling, digits as raw code points
  ('Track 10' sorted before 'Track 2'). cave_pfx reads the
  record's full name via the string index the builder stored
  at record+0xc immediately before this loop (same address
  formula and module-0 read call 0x03067510 the comparator
  uses), invalidates both comparator string-cache slots so
  the scratch reuse cannot serve stale strings, and writes
  the first 4 units of the full sort transform (casefold +
  Latin-1 accent fold + 'The ' strip + natural-number tokens)
  to record+4..+0xa, exactly where stock wrote its prefix.
